  "question": {
    "text": "An elastic spring under tension of $3 \\mathrm{~N}$ has a length $a$. Its length is $b$ under tension $2 \\mathrm{~N}$. For its length $(3 a-2 b)$, the value of tension will be______$\\mathrm{N}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 3=\\mathrm{K}(\\mathrm{a}-\\ell) \\\\ & 2=\\mathrm{K}(\\mathrm{b}-\\ell) \\\\ & \\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{K}(3 \\mathrm{a}-2 \\mathrm{~b}-\\ell) \\\\ & \\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{K}(3(\\mathrm{a}-\\ell)-2(\\mathrm{~b}-\\ell) \\\\ & =\\mathrm{K}\\left[3\\left(\\frac{3}{\\mathrm{~K}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{~K}}\\right)\\right] \\\\ & =9-4 \\\\ & =5 \\mathrm{~N}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}